      "why_it_failed": "The current engine executes one bounded throw-compensation end-event subset: the event must run inside one supported transaction shell and must either reference one explicit `activityRef` that reuses an already valid boundary-to-handler compensation binding for that target activity or omit `activityRef` to replay every already compensable activity in reverse completion order. The event may stay synchronous or set `waitForCompletion=\"false\"` so the parent scope resumes while the bounded compensation queue drains. Any other end-event throw-compensation shape remains unsupported.",
      "repair_guidance": [
        "If compensation is really required, remodel the flow so the throwing end event lives inside one bounded transaction shell.",
